SUMMARY:Step Into the World of Vector Control: Free Family-Friendly Open House
DESCRIPTION:Step behind the scenes and discover how the Marin/Sonoma Mosquito and Vector Control District works year-round to protect public health. This free\, family-friendly event invites residents of all ages to explore hands-on activities\, interactive displays\, and live demonstrations that highlight the District’s Integrated Vector Management Program. \nEducational displays will showcase mosquito and tick surveillance methods used to identify and prevent emerging threats to public health\, non-toxic rodent control strategies\, and simple tips for reducing mosquito sources around the home. \nGuests can learn how mosquito traps work\, meet the vector control technicians who respond to service requests\, and leave with practical\, easy-to-use information to help protect their families and neighborhoods. \nWhether you are stopping by to learn\, ask questions\, or enjoy a day of discovery\, the District’s Open House offers a welcoming opportunity to connect with the people dedicated to keeping Marin and Sonoma counties safe from mosquitoes and vector-borne diseases. \n– Kid-friendly activities (balloon animals\, bounce house\, games and prizes)\n– Field equipment will be on display (airboat\, ARGOs\, and more)\n– Live tick and mosquito displays\n– Tick-bite prevention tips and free tick removers\n– Information about non-toxic rodent control and prevention\n– Educational displays about yellowjackets and honey bees\n– Free lunch and refreshments
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/step-into-the-world-of-vector-control-free-family-friendly-open-house/
LOCATION:Marin/Sonoma Mosquito and Vector Control District\, 595 Helman Lane\, Cotati\, 94931
CATEGORIES:Festival,Kids and Family,Other
END:VEVENT
